  "slug": "omics-biopsies-9eab",
  "summary": "Recent tools package multi-step analyses into portable, modular software, carrying reproducibility in the packaging itself.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is packaging multi-step analyses into modular, reproducible software. Utanos and the PMBB Geno-Pheno Toolkit are containerized Nextflow pipelines, with the PMBB toolkit running across HPC, cloud, and All of Us environments and adding cross-biobank meta-analysis for GWAS, ExWAS, and PheWAS. scGraphVerse modularizes five single-cell gene network inference methods (GENIE3, GRNBoost2, ZILGM, PCzinb, JRF) within one R package, and MLHeatmap wraps normalization, multiclass classification, feature ranking, and heatmap visualization in a browser application. CyFj11 addresses a different interface problem, importing FlowJo v11 gating hierarchies into R and exporting R-defined gates back to FlowJo with population counts matching R-derived values. What is new is the emphasis on portability and workflow-level composition, with reproducibility carried by the software packaging itself.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-07-31"
}
